Martin Read wrote:
> Nethack's worst feature: incredibly dangerous effects you cannot afford
> to be affected by even once, for which there is a perfect boolean defence.

Hmm... the others would be:
* "Touch of Death" monster spell. (Of negligible merit, and removed by
a few patches of mine.)
* Polymorph trap. (I've become doubtful of the merit of this trap type
as well. I think I'll start a topic about it.)
* Cockatrice flesh. (But mostly avoidable through specific behaviour.
Something that doesn't make sense, though, is why sometimes you get a
petrification timeout and most times you petrify instantly.)
* Disintegration attacks. (Reduced somewhat in my Half-resistance
patch.)
* Drowning attacks. (In my opinion both this and "drowning by
levitation loss" should map with the strangulation case.)
* "Destroy armor" monster spell. (Not as inherently dangerous as the
others, but still overpowered.)
* Wand of death.
* Medusa's gaze. (But there are ample opportunites provided to avoid
it.)
* Drawbridges. (But fortunately this is an isolated case.)
* Lava. (But hey, it's _lava._)

P.S: I suppose NetHack's second worst feature would be the treadmills?



